0211: enhanced lighting GPU cost, same picture

- Incremental masks: a frame's second light-shadow/AO mask (a later EFB pass with new opaque
  draws) adds only the new draws to the depth pre-pass (also with AO alone, which re-rendered
  every draw) and recomputes the AO and shadow-map mask texels only within one 8x8 tile of where
  the pre-pass depth changed (fs_dirty: tile flags from the previous and new depth snapshots);
  the rest keeps the frame's previous mask. Only the later pass's own draws read that mask, at
  their own (depth-matched) texels. AURORA_ENH_MASK_FULL=1: every mask complete (A/B).
- Ambient occlusion: no second load of each sample's depth (mask_view_pos re-read it), same in
  the 4x4 blur.
- Shadow-map mask: each light's face matrix is loaded once, not per filter tap.
- Receivers (GX shaders): enh_mask's 16 tap rows and tent x depth-match weights are computed once
  per fragment and shared by every shadowed light and the AO plane (bit-identical sums).
- Realistic flashlight: the shadow map's 2x2 footprint per step is two gathers (the key's bytes)
  instead of four loads; periodic hash modulo by a power of two is a bit mask.

